[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a way to enumerate the elements of a Std.ExtHashMap. Ideally something like Std.HashMap.toList but for ExtHashMap. I noticed that fold is also not present with the note <code>-- TODO: add fold similar to </code>Finset.fold`.</p>",
        "id": 597816683,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779794541
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Operations about ExtHashMap are not allowed to depend on the internal order, so you have to make sure that you get the same result for any hashmap with the same content. This seems only doable if you have a total order on your keys. Then you can do <code>m.toList.mergeSort.enumerate</code> and proof that this is always the same, but this is not really efficient.</p>",
        "id": 597820757,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779795726
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you want an order, you might want to consider a treeMap instead, where you can implement your operation using fold as this has an order by definition.</p>",
        "id": 597821006,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779795805
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The issue is that I depend on the performance characteristics of the HashMap. Specifically constant time access and linear in-place mutations. I am fine with nlog n time for enumeration which would cover sorting.</p>",
        "id": 597821733,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796002
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it important to be an ExtHashMap instead of a normal hash map?</p>",
        "id": 597821903,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779796050
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unfortunately yes because I use ext_getElem? for a proof</p>",
        "id": 597822117,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I need to prove that two ExtHashMaps are equal in a specific circumstance</p>",
        "id": 597822494,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796186
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can use normal hashmaps and show that they are beq. All operations that are defined on extHashMap are the same for beq hashmaps. If they behave the same for all operations, then does it really matter whether they are the same?</p>",
        "id": 597823319,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779796420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well, so far I have built everything on requiring Eq</p>",
        "id": 597823867,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796574
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure if I will be able to then show Eq for the normal hashmaps?</p>",
        "id": 597823992,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796612
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually I think the nature of the proof (considering concurrent inserts) won't work with the normal hashmap anyways because the order <em>will</em> differ</p>",
        "id": 597824440,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796722
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, you won't be able to show Eq for normal hashmaps as they can have different internal representations of the same collection of elements. This representation leaks in operations like toList or fold and thus they are not available for ExtHashMap.</p>",
        "id": 597824498,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779796738
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think a fold given AddCommMonoid for the keys would suffice for my usecase</p>",
        "id": 597824691,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, wait. That is mathlib. Then I mean Std.Associative and Std.Commutative</p>",
        "id": 597824925,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would be willing to put some work into implementing this. Given the presence of the TODO I think this would also be a desired feature?</p>",
        "id": 597825220,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779796918
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would assume so, but I can't officially represent Std. But I don't see how this would help your enumerate case. How would you use fold to enumerate?</p>",
        "id": 597825593,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779797027
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Given a total order over the keys you could implement enumerate with fold</p>",
        "id": 597827721,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797609
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Essentially a sorting algorithm passed to fold</p>",
        "id": 597827768,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797624
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess the other option would be to expose toList such that it sorts the internal representation</p>",
        "id": 597827881,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797650
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the end you need to pass a total order on the keys</p>",
        "id": 597827935,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797670
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"977822\">Alexander Städing</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Enumerate.20ExtHashMap/near/597827721\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Given a total order over the keys you could implement enumerate with fold</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>would this be some kind of insertion sort isn't that quadratic time</p>",
        "id": 597828049,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779797709
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess actually you can put whatever algorithm you want in there that can take one element at time</p>",
        "id": 597828204,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779797760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I need to brush up on sorting algorithms but yes it appears that it would be an insertion sort and quadratic</p>",
        "id": 597828297,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797784
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it possible to implement an nlog n sorting algorithm with fold? I guess not?</p>",
        "id": 597828438,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797827
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Then probably it would be best to expose toList such that it sorts the internal representation and the fold is separate from that</p>",
        "id": 597828563,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779797870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you want to implement fold like for Finset, then the operation must be commutative which is not really the case here.</p>",
        "id": 597829045,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779798006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the sort via fold: I am thinking of fold function that takes two lists and returns a merged sorted list. This would be comm + assoc</p>",
        "id": 597829279,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779798067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But that is not an operation on HashMaps?</p>",
        "id": 597829530,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779798143
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes you would need a lift function. Something like this:<br>\n<code>fold {α : Type} (op : α → α → α) [AddCommMonoid α] (a : α) (lift : (K × V) → α) : α</code></p>",
        "id": 597829771,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779798207
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Although rather more like this for the stdlib: <code>fold {α : Type} (f : α → α → α) [Std.Associative f] [Std.Commutative f] (a : α) (lift : (K × V) → α) : α</code></p>",
        "id": 597830475,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779798416
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And you don't think its easier to make <code>toList</code> work given an order and then use <code>ExtHashMap.ofList (m.toList.enumerate) </code>?</p>",
        "id": 597831194,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1779798600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"619540\">Johannes Tantow</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Enumerate.20ExtHashMap/near/597831194\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And you don't think its easier to make <code>toList</code> work given an order and then use <code>ExtHashMap.ofList (m.toList.enumerate) </code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I do think it would be easier at this point:</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"977822\">Alexander Städing</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Enumerate.20ExtHashMap/near/597828563\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Then probably it would be best to expose toList such that it sorts the internal representation and the fold is separate from that</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 597832476,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779798949
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And most likely also more performant</p>",
        "id": 597832574,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779798973
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it possible to use <code>ExtTreeMap</code> for your purposes? Because it has the advantage that it's already sorted so you can just fold over it and use <code>toList</code> or <code>toArray</code> however you want.</p>",
        "id": 597897312,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779814887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Otherwise,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ExtHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toArraySorted</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Hashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableLE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsLinearOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EquivBEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LawfulHashable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ExtHashMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Const</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toArray_toList</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort_eq_toArray_mergeSort_toList</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injEq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort_perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">constToList_perm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort_perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DHashMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pairwise_mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">and</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">distinct_keys_toList</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort_perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comm</span><span class=\"o\">]))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">perm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq_of_pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">decide_eq_true_eq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597904791,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779817085
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I will give the tree a go, but it will probably be too slow on insert (logarithmic vs constant time for hash map). I understand that this means enumeration will take at least nlog n. </p>\n<p>Thanks for that snippet, it did the trick but I had to switch to a release candidate. It seems there are many new lemmas around mergeSort / Arrays in v4.30-rc2. Unfortunately this stuff is not in a stable release yet</p>",
        "id": 598059321,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Städing",
        "timestamp": 1779880612
